  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>An aromatic compound can follow Huckel&#39;s rule if it has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></math>-electrons</p><p>where, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo></math> integer <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo></math> etc.</p><p>Thus,&nbsp;</p><p>(a) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> follow Huckel&#39;s rule</p><p>(b) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>;</mo></math> Number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></math>-electrons <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> follows Huckels rules.</p><p>(c) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>;</mo></math> Number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></math>-electrons <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> follows Huckel&#39;s rule.</p><p>(d) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, Number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></math>-electrons <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>but this compound has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math> electrons which distorts the plane and hence does not follows Huckel&#39;s rule.</p>"
  }
